   "text": "I read the drawing as a macrocycle assembled from five parts, and wrote the SMILES in that order.\n\n- **Piperazic ester:** a hexahydropyridazine ring whose C3 carbon carries the ester C=O. Its ring N1 is acylated.\n- **Linker:** the ester oxygen is joined through CH2\u2013C(CH3)2\u2013CH2 to C3 of the indole.\n- **Indole:** N-ethyl, with a 2-(1-methoxyethyl)pyridin-3-yl group on C2 and the thiazole on C5.\n- **Thiazole and side chain:** thiazole C4 bonds to indole C5. Thiazole C2 carries CH2\u2013CH(NHC(=O)-cyclopropyl)\u2013C(=O), and that carbonyl closes the ring onto the piperazic N1.\n- **Cyclopropane:** a 2-methylcyclopropane-1-carboxamide.\n\nAll five stereocentres are labelled S in the drawing. I assigned each @/@@ by working out the CIP priorities. The piperazic C3 needed @@, and the other four came out as @, @, @@ and @ in the order they appear in the string.\n\nSMILES: O=C1OCC(C)(C)Cc2c(-c3cccnc3[C@H](C)OC)n(CC)c3ccc(cc23)-c2csc(n2)C[C@H](NC(=O)[C@H]2C[C@@H]2C)C(=O)N2CCC[C@@H]1N2"
